# Review ownership (project sheet §6, D7; team proposal §4.2 CR-assignment system).
#
# HOW CODEOWNERS RESOLVES OWNERS: a changed file is owned by the **last matching pattern**,
# not by the union of every pattern that matches. Order therefore matters — broad rules must
# come first, specific rules after them, or the specific rule is shadowed.
#
# Each rule lists TWO owners — the domain owner plus one fallback — so that any rule stays
# satisfiable when the domain owner is the PR author: GitHub forbids self-approval, and with
# `require_code_owner_reviews` enabled the approval has to come from an owner of the file.
#
# Machine-enforced: branch protection on `main` has `require_code_owner_reviews: true`, so
# these approvals are required in addition to the generic "1 non-author approving review".
# Per-domain review duties and the memo format live in docs/review-memo.md; member guide:
# .github/CONTRIBUTING.md.

# Default: PM + governance & CI owner. Must stay FIRST — every rule below overrides it.
*                          @swordnew123 @creator-xiyuan

